30 languages, it's crushing.
- Huge, (blows raspberry)

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.353
that's a huge number.

00:10:02.353 --> 00:10:05.370
- But I sell that book to a publisher,

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.810
who sells that book to Amazon,

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.010
Amazon's now responsible for 80% or so

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.100
of book sales--
- That's it?

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.420
- Of, so that you basically

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.930
sell your book to a middleman.
- No, that wasn't a joke.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:15.958
- You think it should be higher?

00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:18.220
- (laughs) No, I don't think it should.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.053
- Great.
- First of all, I don't think

00:10:19.053 --> 00:10:20.510
anything should, second--

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.610
- Your guess would be higher.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:22.950
- No, I mean, that's a pretty

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.420
ridiculous number.
- It's insane.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.220
- It's a joke to everybody
who competes against Amazon

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.053
